 "splits": {
  "25": [
   {
    "text": "Dude, look at me. Look at me.",
    "speaker": "Young Skinner"
   },
   {
    "text": "Everybody's scared.",
    "speaker": "Young Skinner"
   }
  ],
  "59": [
   {
    "text": "Sir, of whom are we speaking?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "Cut the crap, agents.",
    "speaker": "Alvin Kersh"
   }
  ],
  "74": [
   {
    "text": "Sir, has anyone checked his apartment?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Could he have had a medical emergency?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "107": [
   {
    "text": "Is that a--?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "Desiccated human ear.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "112": [
   {
    "text": "...my only concern here is for Skinner.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "But now I'm worried about him.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "118": [
   {
    "text": "...like names of his fellow Marines, et cetera...",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Uh-huh.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "127": [
   {
    "text": "Doctor Matthew Wegweiser.",
    "speaker": "Sheriff Stenzler"
   },
   {
    "text": "The victim was a medical doctor?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "133": [
   {
    "text": "A hunting trap?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "How do you account for the severed ear?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "135": [
   {
    "text": "Missing teeth?",
    "speaker": "Sheriff Stenzler"
   },
   {
    "text": "The autopsy says that he was missing...",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "158": [
   {
    "text": "Is Glazebrook a mental hospital?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Right, ma'am, a government-run facility.",
    "speaker": "Sheriff Stenzler"
   }
  ],
  "161": [
   {
    "text": "But I'll see what I can drum up.",
    "speaker": "Sheriff Stenzler"
   },
   {
    "text": "Thank you, sheriff.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "244": [
   {
    "text": "What?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "You said trigger.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "292": [
   {
    "text": "His records were sealed, even from me.",
    "speaker": "Walter Skinner"
   },
   {
    "text": "Who vanished him?",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "371": [
   {
    "text": "Is your father home?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "No, I'm sorry. I haven't a clue where he is.",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "389": [
   {
    "text": "No, no, I'm good.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "No, thank you.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "393": [
   {
    "text": "On what grounds?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Sorry?",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "402": [
   {
    "text": "What did you mean?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Father had secrets.",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "403": [
   {
    "text": "Secrets?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "About the government.",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "407": [
   {
    "text": "What kind of tests?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "Chemical and biological.",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "413": [
   {
    "text": "And they still haven't perfected it.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "But after years of testing it and honing it...",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   }
  ],
  "414": [
   {
    "text": "...they are getting close.",
    "speaker": "Davey James"
   },
   {
    "text": "To what end?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "464": [
   {
    "text": "Mulder?",
    "speaker": "Walter Skinner"
   },
   {
    "text": "Skinner.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ]
 },
 "text": {
  "23": "You all right, John?\nI'm scared as hell, man!",
  "37": "[MAN SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]",
  "66": "...in the event that there are any questions about this in your conspiracy-addled minds.",
  "68": "...has everything to do with his blind loyalty to the both of you...",
  "79": "I couldn't say. But if you truly care about his future in the FBI...",
  "83": "...it's safe to say the old Skinner has left the building.",
  "87": "But I'll keep my eyes peeled for cigarette butts.",
  "92": "...no family photographs.",
  "99": "As much as I don't trust the guy right now...",
  "100": "...if he's gotten into a dangerous situation, he's gonna forgive us this little trespass.",
  "104": "That's a peculiar way to address it.",
  "128": "That's correct, ma'am. Doc Wegweiser is-- Was our one and only town doctor.",
  "145": "Yes, ma'am. It was a primitive whip trap.",
  "173": "Pippet. What is it, girl?",
  "202": "...so it shouldn't take terribly long to find what we're looking for.",
  "207": "Why do I get the distinct feeling you two know who that man is?",
  "224": "Well, I know it looks bad, sheriff, but I assure you, he's not your man.",
  "225": "You can assure me all you want. I'll decide who my man is...",
  "249": "I told the eagle where to find Kitten's kitten.\nThe eagle. Hmm.",
  "261": "...I slice this little monster's ear off like a hunk of Wisconsin cheddar.",
  "269": "[SOLDIERS 2 AND 3 GROAN]",
  "291": "I spent years searching for him after his trial, but they vanished him.",
  "325": "And I know it was because of the gas. I knew who he was before.",
  "343": "...is he's a man ruled by his moral compass above all else.",
  "348": "I mean, especially in light of what we now understand he may have sacrificed for us.",
  "363": "Why?",
  "366": "Special Agent Mulder. Special Agent Dana Scully.",
  "383": "...music...",
  "434": "Thank you, sir.",
  "470": "I'll boost you up. I'll boost you, you're good.",
  "504": "...he didn't enlist.",
  "507": "...by a war that he really, truly didn't even understand.",
  "512": "...it put a dent in that blind faith that I had in my government.",
  "521": "...or to throw in with you two, make no mistake about it..."
 },
